 "version": 1,
 "title": "Warm Analog Strings",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: the warm, lush string-machine pad of 70s and 80s synth records: slow-bowed 'strings' made of detuned saws, swimming in ensemble chorus.\n\nHow it's built: two saws a little apart, through a soft Ladder filter; a slow attack and release; the Chorus in Ensemble mode does most of the work (it's what made string machines sound like strings); a Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: slow chords, long notes.\n\nTweak: the envelope's ATTACK and RELEASE, the second oscillator's TUNE, the filter's CUTOFF (darker is more distant).",
